<p class="mt-2 text-secondary text-body-sm">
  Entry to the competition costs <b>50,000 COP</b>, transferred to the app
  administrator. The amount is split: <b>30,000 COP</b> for Polla mode and
  <b>20,000 COP</b> for Fantasy mode.
</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-secondary text-body-sm">
  The competition closes on the day of the World Cup final, and prizes will
  be paid out to the winners within <b>7 days of the competition
  closing</b>. There is a <b>maximum of 12 participants</b>, and everyone
  must be registered before the World Cup's first match kicks off to be
  eligible for prizes. All participants compete in both modes, Polla and
  Fantasy, and the amount collected is split between both modes as described
  above.
</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-secondary text-body-sm">
  Each app has its own leaderboard, and the money is awarded to the first-
  and second-place finishers of each mode as follows: second place receives
  that mode's entry cost, and first place receives the rest of the amount.
</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-secondary text-body-sm">
  <i>Example:</i> With <b>12</b> participants, the total amount collected
  would be <b>600,000 COP</b>. Of that, <b>360,000 COP</b>
  would go to Polla and <b>240,000 COP</b> to Fantasy. In Polla, second
  place would receive <b>30,000 COP</b> and first place would receive
  <b>330,000 COP</b>. In Fantasy, second place would receive <b>20,000
  COP</b> and first place would receive <b>220,000 COP</b>.
</p>
